# Use this file to define individuals or teams that are responsible for code in a repository.
# Read more: <https://help.github.com/articles/about-codeowners/>
#
# Order is important: the last matching pattern has the highest precedence

# These owners will be the default owners for everything
*             @openevidence/core-engineering

# Core Engineering must review any changes to Makefiles
**/Makefile   @openevidence/core-engineering
**/Makefile.* @openevidence/core-engineering

# Core Engineering must review any changes to GitHub actions
.github/*     @openevidence/core-engineering

# Core Engineering must review any changes to standard context definition,
# but some changes can be rubber-stamped.
**/*.tf       @openevidence/core-engineering
README.yaml   @openevidence/core-engineering
README.md     @openevidence/core-engineering
docs/*.md     @openevidence/core-engineering

# Core Engineering must review all changes to CODEOWNERS or the mergify configuration
.github/mergify.yml @openevidence/core-engineering
.github/CODEOWNERS  @openevidence/core-engineering
